.*
.* QSQSICSL: the QSI server's management consoles (docs/QSID.md section
.* 12). STRQSIPAIR's pairing password, shown once, and WRKQSICSL's list
.* of the consoles paired. QS/400's own displays, laid out as the
.* system's others are.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=HALFCL BASETYPE='CHAR 32'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PWDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 19'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STAMPCL BASETYPE='CHAR 18'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NUMCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=DATECL BASETYPE='CHAR 14'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SHORTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 16'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FULLCL BASETYPE='CHAR 64'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=FPRINT1 CLASS=HALFCL.
:VAR NAME=FPRINT2 CLASS=HALFCL.
:VAR NAME=PASSWORD CLASS=PWDCL.
:VAR NAME=UNTIL CLASS=STAMPCL.
:VAR NAME=ATTEMPTS CLASS=NUMCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=CNAME CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PAIRED CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=LASTSES CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=FPSHORT CLASS=SHORTCL.
:VAR NAME=FPFULL CLASS=FULLCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=CONSOLES VARS='OPT CNAME PAIRED LASTSES FPSHORT FPFULL'.
:KEYL NAME=PAIRKEYS HELP=PAIRKEYH.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=End the password
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=CSLKEYS HELP=CSLKEYH.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=QSIPAIR KEYL=PAIRKEYS HELP=QSIPAIRH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Start QSI Pairing
:DATA DEPTH=6.
:DATACOL WIDTH=36.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=FPRINT1 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FPRINT'.System's QSI fingerprint
:DATAI VAR=FPRINT2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FPRINT'.
:DATAI VAR=PASSWORD USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/PASSWORD'.Pairing password
:DATAI VAR=UNTIL USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/UNTIL'.Good until
:DATAI VAR=ATTEMPTS USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/ATTEMPTS'.Attempts
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Type the password at the management console. It is shown once.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=QSICSL KEYL=CSLKEYS HELP=QSICSLH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Work with QSI Consoles
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=36.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=FPRINT1 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FPRINT'.System's QSI fingerprint
:DATAI VAR=FPRINT2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FPRINT'.
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=CONSOLES SCROLL=YES MAXHEAD=2.(No consoles are paired)
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD RMVQSICSL CONSOLE(&FPFULL.)' HELP='QSICSL/OPTIONS'.4=Remove
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='QSICSL/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=CNAME USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/CNAME'.Console
:LISTCOL VAR=PAIRED USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/PAIRED'.Paired
:LISTCOL VAR=LASTSES USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/LASTSES'.Last session
:LISTCOL VAR=FPSHORT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FPSHORT'.Fingerprint
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=QSIPAIRH.Start QSI Pairing - Help
:P.A one-time pairing password for a management console, shown on
this display and nowhere else. Type it at the console as it pairs with
this system; the console checks the fingerprint shown here. The
password is good for one pairing, for the time shown and for the
attempts shown; a new one replaces it. This display is QS/400's own.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=PAIRKEYH.Function keys - Help
:P.Enter and F3 leave the password out until it is used or it
expires. F12 ends it at once.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=QSICSLH.Work with QSI Consoles - Help
:P.The management consoles paired with this system, at most two, and
the system's own fingerprint, which a console shows as it pairs. A
console is trusted by its certificate's fingerprint and nothing else.
This display is QS/400's own.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CSLKEYH.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave, F5 reads the list again.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FPRINT'.System's QSI fingerprint
:P.The SHA-256 of the system's QSI certificate, in hexadecimal, made
the first time the QSI server started. A console shows it as it pairs:
compare the two before typing the password.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PASSWORD'.Pairing password
:P.Sixteen characters in four groups. Dashes and spaces do not matter
when typed, nor upper or lower case.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/UNTIL'.Good until
:P.When the password expires, fifteen minutes after it was made.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ATTEMPTS'.Attempts
:P.How many tries the password is good for; a wrong one uses a try.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSICSL/OPT'.Opt
:P.Type the number of an option next to a console and press Enter.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='QSICSL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.4=Remove removes the console's pin, as RMVQSICSL does: a session it
has ends and it cannot connect again until it is paired again.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CNAME'.Console
:P.The name the console gave when it paired.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PAIRED'.Paired
:P.When the console paired.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LASTSES'.Last session
:P.When the console last had a session with this system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FPSHORT'.Fingerprint
:P.The first sixteen hexadecimal digits of the console's certificate's
fingerprint; RMVQSICSL takes the whole of it.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
